<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">THE DARK CODEX / ACTIVE DIRECTORY</p><h1>Impacket<span>.</span></h1><p class="lead">Python tools for SMB, Kerberos, and Windows protocols. Impacket is a toolkit of protocol implementations and example utilities used for Windows/AD assessment.</p></header>
<img class="hero-img" src="/images/dark-codex/impacket.png" alt="Impacket Dark Codex cover" loading="eager" width="768" height="256" />
<div class="note"><strong>Scope:</strong> These examples are intended for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. Replace placeholders with lab values. CLI options can change between releases; check each tool's <code>--help</code> output.</div>
<div class="body-grid"><article>
<section class="section" id="commands"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FIELD COMMANDS</p><h2>Commands you'll actually use</h2><div class="examples"><div class="example"><h3>Explore SMB shares</h3><p>Open an interactive SMB client with authorized credentials.</p><pre><code>impacket-smbclient &lt;domain&gt;/&lt;user&gt;:&lt;password&gt;@&lt;target&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>List service principal names</h3><p>List user-linked SPNs in the domain.</p><pre><code>impacket-GetUserSPNs &lt;domain&gt;/&lt;user&gt;:&lt;password&gt; -dc-ip &lt;dc-ip&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Review Kerberos pre-auth settings</h3><p>Query accounts and Kerberos pre-authentication behavior.</p><pre><code>impacket-GetNPUsers &lt;domain&gt;/&lt;user&gt;:&lt;password&gt; -dc-ip &lt;dc-ip&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Request a TGT</h3><p>Request a Kerberos ticket for a permitted account.</p><pre><code>impacket-getTGT &lt;domain&gt;/&lt;user&gt;:&lt;password&gt; -dc-ip &lt;dc-ip&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Tool-specific help</h3><p>Check flags, output options, and packaging differences.</p><pre><code>impacket-GetUserSPNs -h</code></pre></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="concepts"><p class="eyebrow">02 / REMEMBER THIS</p><h2>Key concepts and flags</h2><div class="terms"><div class="term"><strong>Tool naming</strong><p>Some installations expose impacket-ToolName; others provide ToolName.py.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>SPNs</strong><p>Service principal names identify services in Kerberos.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Kerberos</strong><p>Time, DNS, and domain-controller reachability matter.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="workflow"><p class="eyebrow">03 / FIELD NOTES</p><h2>Practical reminders</h2><ul><li>Use a test account and avoid placing real passwords in published command history.</li><li>Impacket includes more invasive utilities; this quick reference focuses on common discovery and authentication.</li></ul></section>
<section class="section sources" id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SOURCES & CREDITS</p><h2>Documentation and attribution</h2><p>This is an independently written PentestBlueprint quick reference informed by the official project documentation below. Tool names and trademarks belong to their respective projects; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/fortra/impacket" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Impacket official repository ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/fortra/impacket/blob/master/examples/GetUserSPNs.py" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GetUserSPNs source ↗</a></li></ul></section>
</article><aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong><a href="#commands">Common commands</a><a href="#concepts">Key concepts</a><a href="#workflow">Field reminders</a><a href="#sources">Sources & credits</a></aside></div>
